<!--
  Every public page, and every public page is in here.

  **This list and `src/lib/page-heads.ts` are the same set, asserted both ways** by
  src/lib/document-head.test.ts. A `<loc>` with no head, or a head with no `<loc>`, fails the
  build — which is the point: the sitemap saying "index these" while a canonical said "index the
  home page instead" is the bug that once excluded four real pages from Google.

  Twenty URLs. Hand-written rather than generated, because they change only when someone adds a
  marketing page and a generator would be more machinery than the thing it produces. If a blog
  ever arrives, generate it then.

  /login, /signup and /onboarding are deliberately absent, and are `Disallow`ed in robots.txt. A
  sign-in form is not a search result anyone wants, and an indexed one competes with the home
  page for the brand query.

  `lastmod` is the date the page's copy last changed, not a build timestamp. A date that moves on
  every deploy teaches crawlers to ignore it.
-->
